From fc4e1255154ea67e82963d38e1aac755ab5b9c43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kob <kob@invalid>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:50:17 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Pools survive a provider swap; replaced pools close before
 successors connect

Pool clones are handles to one pool, so Client::replace can keep unchanged pools.
A pool left out is retired: idle connections close at once, busy ones once their
requests are answered, and it takes no new requests. Pools of one account share
a connection semaphore (Pool::with_account), so a successor opens connections
only as its predecessor closes them. Downloads::resize changes the shared slot
count in place, so requests on old and new pools share one limit.
